From ffd9cb699b0595e200c937058c10e5932c7fa519 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Idogun <sirneij@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 06:36:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 03/17] Add SingleStore support (singlestore_rules,
 solve_with_singlestore)

SingleStore requires UNION ALL between base and recursive term and forbids
DISTINCT/UNION in the recursive term, so the closure is computed as
SELECT DISTINCT over all paths, with max_recursive_cte_iterations raised
from 32 to 10000. Results are fetched through the client because
INTO OUTFILE writes inside the server container.
